    "body": "Not using `[Unscopable]` seems fine to me.\r\n\r\nI only feel a little strongly about whether we return the node operated on or not. Personally I prefer as much consistency with `insertBefore()`, and I think it makes the API more ergonomic. That's why I like `appendChild()` compared to `append()`, personally: I like seeing `const iframe = document.appendChild(document.createElement('iframe'))`. But if Anne feels strongly, I'm happy to remove the return value.",
